  "RUNG-WIDE PROPERTY: every gate on this rung must be able\nto BLOCK from OUTSIDE the model. advisory output is not a\ncheck. this is what makes the escalation contract\ntrustworthy: the human can only afford to hear nothing\nif nothing bad can pass silently.",
  "The whole change, reviewed unanchored",
  "Tony, 2026-08-03: 'im\nchecking it as the\nexpert user.'",
  "code \u00b7 logic \u00b7 architecture \u00b7 pixel vs the approved design \u00b7 the\nproduct measurements from stage 1. each layer reports its own\nconformance; a single green tick is how gaps hide.",
  "every piece landed",
  "no human key per piece. a failing piece is re-dispatched, re-scored,\nor stopped BY THE ROLES \u2014 the human hears nothing unless a gap no\nagent role can answer becomes a BLOCKER (the escalation contract).\npieces loop here until every piece has landed.",
  "on-demand COLD EYES may\nbe ordered early for a\nrisky piece \u2014 one carrying\na countermeasure, or\ntouching fatal terrain.",
  "the flaw class this catches is a gap in\nthe DECLARED TRUTH itself \u2014 'never\ncontacts your server' failed no check,\nbecause nothing declared it. those gaps\nlive at ASSEMBLY, not per piece.",
  "the measured failure this guards: a\ndeletion range that swallowed three\nhelpers while passing every check\nwritten for the piece itself.",
  "the piece arrived with\nits check already written\n\u2014 a piece without one was\nnever handable at all.",
  "the piece's own criteria PLUS everything its change touches \u2014\nrelevance scoped by the overseer, who holds all truth. tests match\nthe acceptance criteria / goal the work order carries.",
  "the reviewing eyes see ONLY the work order and the change \u2014 no build\ncontext, no session memory. the builder's own context is what blinds\nit. once per goal, never routinely per piece.",
